<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 55 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 55 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 55 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.35 BLN   1.5 BLN    1.6 BLN    1.6 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    699 MLN#   1.149 BLN! 1.394 BLN  1.449 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   160 MLN*   141 MLN*     89 MLN*  =</p>
<p> BAND 1  T-BILLS	=		1 MLN*	1 MLN*  =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	     78 MLN*    155 MLN*  =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE				   55 MLN</p>
<p># INC 539 MLN STG BILLS/FRG FOR RESALE OCT 14 AT 5-23/32 PCT ! INCLUDES FURTHER 230 MLN STG BILLS/FRG FOR RESALE OCT 14 AT 5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
